### One-time setup — only if your knowledge base doesn't already have a FILE knowledge source.
### Run with the VS Code REST Client extension or Visual Studio's .http support.
### Afterwards, add the knowledge source to your knowledge base (Foundry portal > Build > Knowledge).

@search-endpoint = https://<your-search-service>.search.windows.net
@api-key = <search-service-admin-key>
@ks-name = sharepoint-docs
@aoai-endpoint = https://<your-foundry-resource>.openai.azure.com
@aoai-embedding-deployment = text-embedding-3-large
@aoai-embedding-model = text-embedding-3-large

### Check what exists (look for "kind": "file")
GET {{search-endpoint}}/knowledgesources?api-version=2026-08-01-preview&$select=name,kind
api-key: {{api-key}}

### Create the file knowledge source
# The search service's managed identity needs "Cognitive Services User" on the Foundry resource
# to call the embedding model.
PUT {{search-endpoint}}/knowledgesources/{{ks-name}}?api-version=2026-08-01-preview
api-key: {{api-key}}
Content-Type: application/json
Prefer: return=representation

{
  "name": "{{ks-name}}",
  "kind": "file",
  "description": "Documents mirrored from the SharePoint shared library every 15 minutes.",
  "fileParameters": {
    "ingestionParameters": {
      "embeddingModel": {
        "kind": "azureOpenAI",
        "azureOpenAIParameters": {
          "resourceUri": "{{aoai-endpoint}}",
          "deploymentId": "{{aoai-embedding-deployment}}",
          "modelName": "{{aoai-embedding-model}}"
        }
      },
      "contentExtractionMode": "minimal"
    }
  }
}

### Inspect what the function has synced
GET {{search-endpoint}}/knowledgesources/{{ks-name}}/files?api-version=2026-08-01-preview
api-key: {{api-key}}
